{{ImageSplit|image=Kraken_artwork.jpg|alt=Kraken|text=The '''Kraken''' is one of the seven major world bosses. It spawns in the Arcadian Sea at set times and stays spawned for 2hrs. It is one of the most valuable bosses in the game.

{{InfoGrid|
{{InfoCard|title=Where|type=info|tag=Arcadian Sea|The Kraken spawns in the western Arcadian Sea. There are 2 potential spawn locations.}}
{{InfoCard|title=When|type=control|tag=Set times|The Kraken spawns at {{LocalTime|13:30|tz=UTC-5|day=Monday}} and {{LocalTime|21:30|tz=UTC-5|day=Wednesday}}.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Primal Kraken|type=danger|tag=Saturdays|A stronger version, the [[Primal Kraken]], rises only on Saturdays at {{LocalTime|16:30|tz=UTC-5|day=Saturday}} and has new mechanics.}}
}}
}}

== Preparation ==
{{InfoGrid|
{{InfoCard|title=Required|type=danger|tag=Ships|wide=yes|The Kraken is immune to all damage except Siege damage, so ships with cannons are needed to kill it. Bring at least 2 galleons with high grade ship cannons.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Required|type=danger|tag=Player|wide=yes|Bring {{Item|ItemID=29300|amount=3}} and {{Item|ItemID=19401}} or {{Item|ItemID=27784}}. <br>
Bring a mount with {{SkillLink|17576}} to survive Kraken's Slam ability.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Optional|type=reward|tag=Aquatic Mounts|Bring a few water mounts (in case they die) such as {{Item|ItemID=8001231}} or {{Item|ItemID=9002331}}.}}
}}

== The fight ==
The Kraken is fought in the open water. Most players swim there, because PvP almost always breaks out and the few cannons on each ship fill up quickly.

{{InfoGrid|
{{InfoCard|title=Aggro|type=control|tag=Tank|The Kraken chases whoever holds aggro, usually a healer. The healer shells the Kraken first to gain aggro, then jumps into the water and keeps it by healing. They tank the Kraken away from the ships so the ships can shell it safely. Nothing but Siege damage hurts the Kraken, so cannons and healing are the only ways to hold its attention.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Ships|type=info|tag=Siege damage|Galleons with high grade ship cannons deal the damage. Aim for 2 or more galleons shelling the Kraken.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Kraken's Slam|type=danger|tag=Avoid|A huge area attack that kills anyone caught inside it. Use a mount with an invincibility skill as soon as you see the Slam animation start. It has a 1 minute cooldown.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Kraken's Gnaw|type=danger|tag=Big hit|Charges at its target and deals a big hit of Siege and Magic damage around it, which also inflicts Electric Shock. It has a 15 second cooldown.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Kraken Ink Splash|type=control|tag=Pull|Pulls everyone nearby towards the Kraken. It has a 45 second cooldown.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Kraken's Tsunami|type=debuff|tag=Aggro swap|Dives forward and deals Magic damage to its target and four other enemies, who are hit with the Electrocution debuff. When it ends the aggro moves to a random player within 200m for 20 seconds. It has a 45 second cooldown.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Kraken's Frenzy|type=heal|tag=Under 30%|Once the Kraken is below 30% health it casts Frenzy, which greatly increases its health regeneration, turn speed and all damage except Siege damage for 5 minutes.}}
}}

{{CallOut|title=Tips|
* Keep the player holding aggro alive in the water.
* Have 2 or more galleons with high grade cannons ready before the fight starts.
* Watch for the Slam animation or cast and dodge it with an invincibility mount.
}}

